Adapted to seasonal semiarid conditions; plant an identified seedling or grafted cultivar at the onset of reliable rain with ample canopy room, commonly 8–10 m. Protect young plants from grazing and provide establishment water. Drought tolerance comes from the developed root system, not from neglecting a new planting. Grafted plants can bear earlier; seedling juvenility is longer. Harvest full-sized green-to-yellow fruit according to fresh or pulp use, picking repeatedly and handling gently. Preserve native vegetation and pollinators. Renew with selected healthy material and retain local adaptation.
} r_1DBRF0MEVQD3JY38JKX2XMF15T

