} r_2735X9Z2PCHZ3YADZ07PXSQKXP

Carambola — Averrhoa carambola (@averrhoa-carambola: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-tropical-fruit, #source @farm-source-carambola, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-190) { r_6Q19ZN1BD8AS22BT0STVNZCDMC
Plant a named grafted cultivar in a warm wind-protected site, around 4–6 m apart. Irrigate through dry periods, mulch, and maintain a low open canopy. Initial crops may appear in 1–3 years. Pick yellowing fruit at appropriate firmness; ribs bruise easily and fruit sweetness depends on cultivar and harvest maturity. Cool and handle gently, and remove infested fallen fruit. Renew through selected nursery stock. Carambola is unsuitable for people with kidney disease; this harvest guide does not establish dietary suitability.
} r_6Q19ZN1BD8AS22BT0STVNZCDMC

