} r_6M6D5NEP5TD3WR5JXQQS7W6R7B

Sour orange — Citrus × aurantium (@citrus-aurantium: 0, is #cultivated-hybrid, #part-of @farming-tropical-fruit, #source @farm-source-tropical-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-210, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-211) { r_45GPS3XG3X3MXHVF8F65Z44VY1
Commonly laranja-da-terra; verify cultivar identity. Follow @citrus-sinensis for certified nursery stock, rootstock choice, establishment, water, and disease prevention. Allow adult canopy space rather than planting several citrus species into one crowded hole. Harvest full-sized mature fruit for its intended juice or peel use; external colour alone does not prove internal maturity. Retain named grafted material for predictable harvest, remove rootstock suckers, and renew declining trees. Do not assume the sour-orange fruiting cultivar and a sour-orange rootstock have interchangeable disease suitability.
