} r_0SG6SGAGC991DP8J1TJ09SN8NY

Persimmon — Diospyros kaki (@diospyros-kaki: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-temperate-fruit, #source @farm-source-tree-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-189) { r_0CAZSKWBCWNDEXEMJ7SZ2DQ8J1
Use a named grafted cultivar in a suitable mild-climate drained site, often 4–6 m apart. Cultivars differ in astringency and pollination response; chocolate fruit colour does not by itself establish a non-astringent type. Water during filling and thin heavy loads if needed. First crops usually take several years. Clip fruit at mature colour without tearing the calyx. Astringent cultivars need full softening or a validated de-astringency process before eating; non-astringent types can be firm. Prune for structure and retain cultivar identity in replacements.
