One common green kiwifruit identity; other Actinidia species require different plans. Establish named nursery plants in a climate with suitable chill and frost protection, using a strong trellis and compatible male pollen plants unless a verified self-fertile cultivar changes the requirement. Space and train for the vigorous mature canopy. Water regularly and prune fruiting wood correctly. First crops often take 3–5 years. Harvest by cultivar dry-matter or soluble-solids maturity criteria, then ripen under controlled conditions; soft fruit on the vine is not the only useful harvest stage. Renew trained arms and diseased plants deliberately.
