Williams commonly belongs here; an ambiguous Park entry needs cultivar confirmation. Plant adapted grafted stock with suitable chill and compatible pollen, allowing space for the chosen rootstock. Train, irrigate, thin excessive crops, and manage regional diseases. First crops often take 3–6 years. Many European pears should be picked mature but firm, then conditioned and ripened off the tree; use cultivar-specific maturity signs rather than waiting for soft fruit. Cool sound fruit appropriately. Prune for accessible bearing wood and renew with labelled disease-free stock.
} r_50V685YNC7R67FMYPB7AFPVAM5

