Use a named grafted cultivar whose chilling requirement fits the site; Aurora is a cultivar example. Plant in a sunny drained site with roughly 4–6 m canopy room. Train an open or locally suitable canopy, thin fruit, and maintain water during filling. Peaches bear on suitable one-year shoots, so annual renewal pruning matters. First crops often appear in 2–3 years. Pick by background colour, firmness, aroma, and intended transport time, not red blush alone. Cool gently. Remove mummified fruit and diseased wood, and renew with clean selected stock.
} r_08052MNKEVHPXWXDC33W6Q7X5C

Pomegranate — Punica granatum (@punica-granatum: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-temperate-fruit, #source @farm-source-pomegranate, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-249) { r_1045J0AV78FX4B3EMVNHPJMAST
Plant a named rooted cutting or nursery plant in a warm sunny drained site, about 3–5 m apart. Train a shrub or small tree and remove unwanted basal shoots. Keep water steady during filling: drought followed by heavy irrigation or rain encourages splitting. Initial crops often occur within 2–3 years. Cut mature fruit at cultivar colour and shape before cracking; it does not become sweeter after picking. Store sound fruit under appropriate cool conditions. Prune after harvest or during the locally suitable dormant period and propagate healthy selected material.
} r_1045J0AV78FX4B3EMVNHPJMAST

Grape — Vitis vinifera (@vitis-vinifera: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-temperate-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-256, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-257, #source @farm-source-grape, #source @farm-source-tropical-fruit) { r_2ATYN83BE25Z7V39DKRFC9GVAA
Itália and Rubi are cultivar examples. Use adapted healthy grafted or rooted stock as local pest and rootstock guidance requires. Install the training system before planting; typical vine spacing is around 1.5–3 m but depends on trellis and vigour. Train trunks and arms, prune the correct buds, manage canopy light and humidity, and irrigate without flooding. First useful crops often take 2–3 years. Harvest clusters by flavour, colour, soluble solids, and acidity; grapes do not gain sugar after cutting. Cool and handle gently. Renew fruiting wood through the cultivar's annual pruning cycle.
