Use fresh viable seed or selected nursery stock suited to floodplain or irrigated upland conditions. Establish with reliable moisture; manage clumps and adult spacing through a regional system rather than letting every sucker grow. Initial fruit commonly takes 3–5 years. Harvest mature dark-purple bunches using trained safe access, then handle quickly in clean containers. Pulp requires hygienic washing and validated processing controls; raw appearance does not exclude pathogen contamination. Keep productive stems and healthy successors, preserve surrounding ecological diversity, and avoid sacrificing fruit-bearing palms for a one-off heart harvest.
} r_4T05WRDWGRX9PR8E8A33EEGMW3

Juçara — Euterpe edulis (@euterpe-edulis: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-jucara, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-138) { r_3C9QHQRCWVS19B8MCBV57DW1X8
Single-stemmed Atlantic Forest palm. Use legally sourced fresh seed and appropriate restoration or cultivated stock; establish in the species' suitable shaded-to-managed-light habitat with dependable moisture. Juvenility lasts several years. Mature purple fruit can be harvested without killing the plant, while keeping food for wildlife and seed recruitment. Heart-of-palm harvest removes its only growing point and kills it; native extraction and commercial use require applicable authorization. Prefer @bactris-gasipaes for a deliberately planted repeatable palm-heart system. Keep source provenance and renew through seed, not imaginary basal regrowth.
} r_3C9QHQRCWVS19B8MCBV57DW1X8

Peach palm — Bactris gasipaes (@bactris-gasipaes: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-peach-palm, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-139, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-596) { r_75FBMGV6N4GMSQ2E3PNFSZ4ZVV
Choose nursery material for the objective: low-spine palm-heart cultivars and fruit cultivars differ. Plant in warm humid drained soil with reliable water; follow a designed clump density and sucker-selection system. Palm-heart crops can reach first cut in roughly 18–24 months under suitable management. Cut only stems at target size and retain healthy replacement suckers. Fruit production uses retained mature stems and takes several years; harvest ripe bunches and cook fruit appropriately. Cool palm hearts promptly. Shelf-stable canning needs a validated acidification/thermal process; a home jar recipe is not enough.
} r_75FBMGV6N4GMSQ2E3PNFSZ4ZVV

Coconut — Cocos nucifera (@cocos-nucifera: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-coconut, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-478, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-590, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-591) { r_7GXJG4F7192GEQYWZ22T7B3538
Plant healthy nursery palms of a suitable dwarf, tall, or hybrid type in a frost-free drained site, often 7–9 m apart. Protect the growing point, irrigate establishment, and balance nutrition from soil and leaf advice. Dwarfs may first crop in about 3–4 years; tall types generally take longer. Harvest young nuts for water and fully mature nuts for kernel or oil using different age and husk criteria. Use trained harvesting methods and protect people below. Replace senescent or seriously diseased palms from clean seed stock; a removed single growing point does not regrow.
} r_7GXJG4F7192GEQYWZ22T7B3538

Oil palm — Elaeis guineensis (@elaeis-guineensis: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-oil-palm, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-259) { r_4492M1SZETTG6S3K8BSG3M4SSB
Dendê needs a humid frost-free climate, suitable land, and access to a mill; it is not a small-bed oil crop. Plant selected nursery material at a system designed for adult crowns, commonly around 9 m in triangular layouts. Maintain ground cover, nutrition, and water without converting native habitat. First bunches often occur in 3–4 years. Harvest ripe bunches by cultivar loose-fruit and colour criteria, collect loose fruit, and process promptly to limit oil deterioration. Prune only as needed for productive healthy leaves and access; replant declining stands deliberately.
} r_4492M1SZETTG6S3K8BSG3M4SSB

Babaçu — Attalea speciosa (@attalea-speciosa: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-babassu, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-267, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-592) { r_6H8XTM4K34BKS0T5WM91AN4AX3
The common name can include related Attalea species. Preserve identified productive palms and local regeneration; establishment and first production take years, so plan this as a long-term palm system. Seed or nursery propagation needs locally appropriate dormancy and establishment methods. Manage light and competing vegetation without burning the stand. Collect sound mature fallen fruits regularly. Separate mesocarp flour and kernel-oil processes with clean protected handling; use guarded cracking equipment. Dry kernels promptly and reject mouldy material. Retain fruit for recruitment and renew through viable seed, since a cut single crown cannot resprout.
} r_6H8XTM4K34BKS0T5WM91AN4AX3

Macaúba — Acrocomia aculeata (@acrocomia-aculeata: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-macauba, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-223) { r_0GS5R6Z24WRN2GET0JCDKEAECB
Use identified selected nursery stock; seed dormancy makes casual germination unpredictable. Establish in a suitable warm seasonal climate with spacing designed for large spiny palms and safe access. Control weeds during the slow juvenile phase, water for establishment, and follow local nutrition guidance. Initial bunches commonly take about 4–6 years or longer. Harvest mature fruit using colour and abscission criteria, collect cleanly, and process pulp or kernels promptly. Keep food and oil processing hygienic and protected from mould. Retain productive palms and renew through healthy selected seed or nursery material.
} r_0GS5R6Z24WRN2GET0JCDKEAECB

Tucumã — Astrocaryum aculeatum (@astrocaryum-aculeatum: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-amazon-fruit) { r_5FQGDG8TY4A7CPC2HSVWH2EHH2
One tucumã identity; A. vulgare also supplies foods with that name. Establish identified nursery palms in a suitable warm Amazonian system with adult crown and spiny-trunk access considered. Germination and juvenility can be slow; use reliable nursery methods and plan several years before fruit. Maintain establishment water and weed control. Harvest mature orange fruit at the local species' ripeness stage; handle with protection from spines and process pulp promptly. Retain part of the crop for regeneration and wildlife. Renew through identified viable seed rather than assuming all tucumã stock shares one cultivation method.
} r_5FQGDG8TY4A7CPC2HSVWH2EHH2

Pequi — Caryocar brasiliense (@caryocar-brasiliense: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-semiarid-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-241, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-271) { r_1YG4KGP9SHE93J3GVSATX18VD9
Use legally sourced identified nursery stock suited to the Cerrado; seed dormancy and juvenility complicate propagation. Establish at reliable rainfall with room for a large crown and protect young plants from livestock and fire. Seedling bearing can take many years; selected grafts may shorten it. Collect naturally mature fallen sound fruit frequently and retain enough for regeneration and fauna. Cook and eat the pulp without biting through the hard spiny inner shell. Process promptly and keep oil handling clean. Prune only for justified management and renew with adapted healthy stock.
} r_1YG4KGP9SHE93J3GVSATX18VD9

Brazil nut — Bertholletia excelsa (@bertholletia-excelsa: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-brazil-nut, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-589, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170569) { r_2630M3DDGEDXKVRNK6MSEB14HD
A large long-lived Amazonian tree whose reproduction depends on compatible trees and effective large-bee pollination. Plant identified nursery stock only where climate, land, and long-term canopy space fit; managed enrichment must retain forest function. First crops can take a decade or more from seedlings. Collect mature fallen capsules with protection from heavy falling fruits, then open with appropriate equipment. Dry nuts promptly and control moisture throughout storage: mould and aflatoxin are major quality hazards. Retain regeneration and do not assume a single isolated garden tree will provide a reliable crop.
} r_2630M3DDGEDXKVRNK6MSEB14HD

Paraná pine — Araucaria angustifolia (@araucaria-angustifolia: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-araucaria, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-595) { r_317BS2PA0HPJQTZKYFVD1SVHFZ
Pinhão is its edible seed. Use legally sourced fresh seed or nursery plants suited to the cool humid southern highland climate. Plan large long-lived trees, multiple individuals, and male/female pollination; ordinary seedlings can take well over a decade to bear. Protect establishment against grazing and drought. Collect mature naturally released seed during the locally permitted season, retaining wildlife food and regeneration. Seed is perishable and loses viability when dried excessively; store for food under appropriate cool conditions and cook before eating. Renew through fresh viable seed; this is not an annual nut crop.
} r_317BS2PA0HPJQTZKYFVD1SVHFZ

Olive — Olea europaea (@olea-europaea: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-260, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-520, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-521, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-171413, #source @farm-source-olive) { r_2J4ENB6V0RK0RHDE7RX7WZD8Q1
Plant healthy named cultivars matched to winter chill, summer conditions, and compatible pollination. Use a sunny exceptionally drained site with spacing suited to the chosen training system. Irrigate establishment, prune for light, and monitor local fruit pests. First crops often take 3–5 years. Table olives are picked green or ripe for a validated curing process; raw fruit is very bitter. Oil harvest timing balances yield and flavour and requires prompt milling. Jar preservation needs tested acidity and salt controls. Maintain productive bearing wood and renew with healthy clonal stock.
} r_2J4ENB6V0RK0RHDE7RX7WZD8Q1

Walnut — Juglans regia (@juglans-regia: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-tree-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-597, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170187) { r_0VA7QZ9JM5ESYDRA34YR46VHRC
English walnut, including the USDA entry. Plant adapted grafted cultivars with adequate winter chill and overlapping pollen, in deep draining soil with ample adult space, often 8–12 m. Protect young trees and irrigate during filling. Grafted trees may begin in roughly 4–7 years, while seedlings take longer. Harvest when hulls split and nuts are mature, remove hulls promptly, and dry kernels adequately before cool protected storage. Discard mouldy nuts. Prune for sound structure and keep cultivar and pollen-partner identities when replacing trees.
} r_0VA7QZ9JM5ESYDRA34YR46VHRC

Almond — Prunus dulcis (@prunus-dulcis: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-palms-nuts, #source @farm-source-tree-fruit, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170567, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170158) { r_49A5RMHAS72JZ5THGV1XQDG2B9
